然后是安吉拉。

971
00:38:24.540 --> 00:38:24.920
Yeah.
是啊。

972
00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:28.420
Well, judging from her outfit, Jan aspires to be a whore.
嗯，从她的穿着来看，简是想当个荡妇。

973
00:38:28.420 --> 00:38:29.840
Do you not have a card?
你没有名片吗？

974
00:38:30.200 --> 00:38:31.960
This is like the biggest sass ever.
这简直是史上最刻薄的讽刺。

975
00:38:31.960 --> 00:38:32.600
Oh, look at this.
哦，看看这个。

976
00:38:32.680 --> 00:38:33.120
Look at this.
看看这个。

977
00:38:33.780 --> 00:38:34.580
Angela sass.
安吉拉的刻薄。

978
00:38:34.760 --> 00:38:35.360
Eye roll.
翻白眼。

979
00:38:35.640 --> 00:38:40.580
When Jan says, dress for the job you want, there is an eye roll that I get sent to me.
当简说要为自己想要的工作而着装时，我收到过一个她翻白眼的镜头。

980
00:38:41.680 --> 00:38:43.160
Oh, that's your gift moment.
哦，那是你的礼物时刻。

981
00:38:43.200 --> 00:38:44.220
Yeah, that's my gift moment.
是啊，那是我的礼物时刻。

982
00:38:44.400 --> 00:38:47.200
And then I have this talking head that I'm a professional woman.
然后我有这个采访镜头，说我是一个职业女性。

983
00:38:47.560 --> 00:38:50.240
I'm in the healthiest relationship of my life.
我正处于人生中最健康的恋爱关系中。

984
00:38:50.420 --> 00:38:53.840
You guys, I want you to, if you have an opportunity to re-listen to that.
伙计们，如果你们有机会的话，我希望你们能重听一下那段。

985
00:38:54.360 --> 00:38:59.640
I did this talking head a few times because I guess whenever I said my life, I would sound really Southern.
我录了好几次这个采访，因为我猜每当我提到“我的生活”时，听起来都特别有南方口音。

986
00:38:59.880 --> 00:39:00.460
My life.
我的生活。

987
00:39:00.580 --> 00:39:02.640
So I said, I'm a professional woman.
所以我说，我是一个职业女性。

988
00:39:02.640 --> 00:39:05.120
I'm in the healthiest relationship of my life.
我正处于人生中最健康的恋爱关系中。

989
00:39:06.160 --> 00:39:07.520
So I had to really think about it.
所以我不得不认真思考了一下。

990
00:39:07.620 --> 00:39:09.180
And I can hear it ever so slightly.
我还是能听出一点点口音。

991
00:39:09.180 --> 00:39:16.720
And then, of course, we have this awkward D'Angela avoiding each other as she says that, which I loved.
然后，当然，我们有那个尴尬的安吉拉和简互相回避的镜头，就在她说那话的时候，我超爱那个。

992
00:39:16.820 --> 00:39:17.980
I love that little moment.
我喜欢那个小瞬间。

993
00:39:18.300 --> 00:39:24.960
But yeah, I mean, Angela thinks Jan is dressed kind of skanky for the workplace.
但确实，我的意思是，安吉拉觉得简在职场的穿着有点轻浮。

994
00:39:24.960 --> 00:39:32.380
Well, speaking of Angela and Dwight, when we go back down to the warehouse, Roy is complaining about how women want men to pay for everything.
说到安吉拉和德怀特，当我们回到仓库时，罗伊正在抱怨女人总是想让男人付一切费用。

995
00:39:32.740 --> 00:39:36.720
And Dwight says, yeah, they make you drive them to church the next morning.
德怀特说，是啊，她们还会让你第二天早上开车送她们去教堂。

996
00:39:36.860 --> 00:39:38.040
I mean, gas ain't free.
我的意思是，油费可不便宜。

997
00:39:39.180 --> 00:39:43.700
But you know what I envision is that he drives her there, but he doesn't go in.
但我脑补的画面是，他开车送她过去，但他自己不进去。

998
00:39:43.840 --> 00:39:49.380
So there's just this like muscle car that pulls up in front of the church.
所以就有一辆肌肉车停在教堂前面。

999
00:39:50.140 --> 00:39:54.500
And then Angela gets out and walks in, and Dwight is like, later.
然后安吉拉下车走进去，德怀特就说，回见。

1000
00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:58.180
Well, this is when Daryl says, we need a union.
嗯，这就是达里尔说我们需要工会的时候。

1001
00:39:58.520 --> 00:39:59.520
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

1002
00:39:59.760 --> 00:40:04.360
And I love Craig Robinson's performance in this so much.
而且我非常喜欢克雷格·罗宾逊在这一集里的表演。

1003
00:40:04.360 --> 00:40:13.060
I was texting with Craig because I really wanted him to come on this episode to talk about this moment because he's so good in it.
我之前给克雷格发了短信，因为我真的很想让他来这一集聊聊这个片段，他在里面的表现太棒了。

1004
00:40:13.060 --> 00:40:14.920
He's so good in it, but he's filming.
他演得太好了，但他正在拍戏。

1005
00:40:15.420 --> 00:40:16.220
He's a busy guy.
他是个大忙人。

1006
00:40:16.380 --> 00:40:16.700
And he couldn't do it.
所以他没法过来。

1007
00:40:16.760 --> 00:40:16.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1008
00:40:17.060 --> 00:40:18.740
But he's going to come on in the future, so don't worry.
但他以后会来的，别担心。

1009
00:40:18.800 --> 00:40:20.500
And we actually get a lot of questions from people.
其实我们收到了很多人的提问。

1010
00:40:20.540 --> 00:40:22.040
Are you planning to have everybody on?
你们打算邀请所有人来吗？

1011
00:40:22.360 --> 00:40:22.720
Yes.
是的。

1012
00:40:22.840 --> 00:40:23.820
Yes, we would love that.
没错，我们非常乐意。

1013
00:40:23.980 --> 00:40:24.340
Everyone.
所有人。

1014
00:40:24.560 --> 00:40:24.800
Yes.
是的。

1015
00:40:24.940 --> 00:40:25.680
We're reaching out.
我们正在联系他们。

1016
00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:26.680
Multiple times.
联系了好几次了。

1017
00:40:26.760 --> 00:40:27.360
Don't worry.
别担心。

1018
00:40:27.580 --> 00:40:30.000
We have a few episodes ahead of us.
我们后面还有好几集呢。

1019
00:40:30.360 --> 00:40:31.020
That's right.
没错。

1020
00:40:31.020 --> 00:40:32.540
Hopefully, we'll get a lot of people on.
希望我们能请到很多人来。

1021
00:40:32.820 --> 00:40:40.160
At 13 minutes, 23 seconds during this whole scene about unions, Creed is reading a newspaper.
在13分23秒，也就是关于工会的整场戏里，克里德在看报纸。

1022
00:40:40.960 --> 00:40:43.160
You guys, it's the Scranton Times.
伙计们，那是《斯克兰顿时报》。

1023
00:40:43.600 --> 00:40:44.160
Nice.
不错。

1024
00:40:44.440 --> 00:40:47.700
Because Phil would get the Scranton Times delivered to us.
因为菲尔会给我们订《斯克兰顿时报》。

1025
00:40:47.880 --> 00:40:48.160
Phil Shea.
菲尔·谢伊。

1026
00:40:48.300 --> 00:40:50.200
Phil Shea, prop master.
菲尔·谢伊，道具师。

1027
00:40:50.880 --> 00:40:55.340
And so whenever there was a newspaper anywhere, it was the Scranton Times.
所以无论哪里出现报纸，那一定都是《斯克兰顿时报》。

1028
00:40:55.340 --> 00:40:58.540
And I loved that detail then, and I love it now.
我当时就很喜欢这个细节，现在依然很喜欢。

1029
00:40:58.680 --> 00:40:59.320
I loved it.
我当时特别喜欢。

1030
00:40:59.320 --> 00:41:04.160
I remember reading one one time in the back of a scene, and there had been a really big
我记得有一次在背景里看报纸，当时刚经历了一场特别大的

1031
00:41:04.160 --> 00:41:08.160
snow storm, and I was reading about the snow in Pennsylvania.
暴风雪，我读的内容就是关于宾夕法尼亚州的雪灾。

1032
00:41:08.400 --> 00:41:08.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1033
00:41:09.220 --> 00:41:09.780
All right.
好吧。

1034
00:41:09.940 --> 00:41:12.040
Well, things are about to really heat up.
好了，接下来气氛要变得紧张起来了。

1035
00:41:12.160 --> 00:41:13.960
There's going to be some tension.
会有一些冲突。

1036
00:41:14.320 --> 00:41:14.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1037
00:41:14.620 --> 00:41:15.260
Should we take a break?
我们要休息一下吗？

1038
00:41:15.380 --> 00:41:17.080
Let's take a break, and then we're going to get into it.
休息一下吧，回来我们再深入探讨。

1039
00:41:17.200 --> 00:41:17.500
All right.
好的。

1040
00:41:22.800 --> 00:41:29.380
We are back, but I'm the only one talking because Angela is being silent.
我们回来了，但现在只有我在说话，因为安吉拉沉默不语。

1041
00:41:29.700 --> 00:41:32.140
Angela, I need to talk about your hair today.
安吉拉，我得聊聊你今天的头发。

1042
00:41:32.140 --> 00:41:32.900
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1043
00:41:32.900 --> 00:41:36.980
It is a hot mess.
简直乱成一团了。

1044
00:41:37.220 --> 00:41:38.280
What happened to you?
你这是怎么了？

1045
00:41:38.440 --> 00:41:41.840
I showered this morning before I took Isabel to school.
我今天早上送伊莎贝尔去学校前洗了个澡。

1046
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:42.140
Yeah.
嗯。

1047
00:41:42.260 --> 00:41:44.400
And my goal was to show up here clean.
我的目标就是干干净净地出现在这儿。

1048
00:41:44.760 --> 00:41:45.620
You are clean.
你确实挺干净的。

1049
00:41:45.660 --> 00:41:46.740
That's as far as I got.
我只能做到这一步了。

1050
00:41:46.980 --> 00:41:48.680
So I got Isabel to school on time.
所以我准时把伊莎贝尔送到了学校。

1051
00:41:48.680 --> 00:41:50.040
I was really happy about that.
我对此真的很高兴。

1052
00:41:50.360 --> 00:41:54.220
And I drove here with wet hair, and I was like, oh, I'll freeze.
我顶着湿头发开车过来，心想，噢，我会冻僵的。

1053
00:41:54.220 --> 00:41:55.580
I will freeze there.
我会在那儿冻僵的。

1054
00:41:55.580 --> 00:41:56.460
It's so cold.
太冷了。

1055
00:41:56.460 --> 00:42:00.320
So I kind of put my window down, and I let the wind kind of dry my hair.
所以我把车窗降下来，让风把我的头发吹干。

1056
00:42:00.320 --> 00:42:01.520
This is explaining it all.
这下全解释通了。

1057
00:42:01.780 --> 00:42:06.780
And now I have this wind-dried hair from the freeway.
现在我这头发就是被高速公路上的风吹干的。

1058
00:42:07.740 --> 00:42:08.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1059
00:42:08.420 --> 00:42:08.860
You do.
确实。

1060
00:42:09.040 --> 00:42:09.400
I do.
没错。

1061
00:42:09.560 --> 00:42:10.500
I do, guys.
真的，伙计们。

1062
00:42:10.700 --> 00:42:12.380
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1063
00:42:12.380 --> 00:42:14.300
I feel fantastic.
我感觉棒极了。

1064
00:42:15.560 --> 00:42:17.840
I, you know, I love it.
我，你知道，我喜欢这样。

1065
00:42:18.100 --> 00:42:19.000
You know, I love it.
你知道，我喜欢这样。

1066
00:42:19.000 --> 00:42:21.380
I look like Medusa a little bit.
我看起来有点像美杜莎。

1067
00:42:21.980 --> 00:42:22.560
You know.
你知道的。

1068
00:42:22.560 --> 00:42:25.620
But it's dry, and I'm not cold, and I'm clean.
但头发干了，我不冷，而且我也洗干净了。

1069
00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:27.980
And I got Isabel to school on time.
我还准时把伊莎贝尔送到了学校。

1070
00:42:28.120 --> 00:42:28.440
Goals.
人生目标。

1071
00:42:28.820 --> 00:42:29.280
Okay.
好的。

1072
00:42:29.820 --> 00:42:35.400
When we come back, Michael busts into the women's meeting to tell Jan that the warehouse
当我们回来时，迈克尔闯进了妇女会议，告诉简仓库那边

1073
00:42:35.400 --> 00:42:36.700
wants to start a union.
想要成立工会。

1074
00:42:37.040 --> 00:42:41.140
And Jan is like, Michael, no, there cannot be a union.
简说，迈克尔，不行，绝对不能有工会。

1075
00:42:41.240 --> 00:42:42.820
You didn't agree to this, right, Michael?
你没答应这事儿吧，迈克尔？

1076
00:42:42.920 --> 00:42:47.020
Like, the men in the warehouse weren't chanting, Michael, Michael, just two minutes ago, right?
仓库里的男人们刚才不是还在高喊“迈克尔，迈克尔”吗？

1077
00:42:47.180 --> 00:42:48.920
And he's like, no, I definitely.
他却说，不，我绝对……

1078
00:42:49.660 --> 00:42:52.260
He says something that would have made me go nuts.
他说了一句让我抓狂的话。

1079
00:42:52.260 --> 00:42:54.860
He says, okay, don't be hysterical.
他说，好了，别歇斯底里了。

1080
00:42:55.020 --> 00:42:55.400
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1081
00:42:55.980 --> 00:42:57.660
That's like you need to calm down.
那话就像是在说“你需要冷静点”。

1082
00:42:57.840 --> 00:42:59.460
That's like one of those kind of phrases.
那属于那种典型的短语。

1083
00:42:59.680 --> 00:43:00.300
Yeah, that's a trigger.
是啊，那是个雷点。

1084
00:43:00.940 --> 00:43:02.280
That's a trigger for sure.
那绝对是个雷点。

1085
00:43:02.480 --> 00:43:05.180
And Pam, your reaction is hilarious.
帕姆，你的反应太搞笑了。

1086
00:43:05.180 --> 00:43:07.620
Once again, you have all of these facial reactions.
你又一次贡献了这么多表情包。

1087
00:43:08.100 --> 00:43:10.520
I had so much fun during this episode.
拍这一集我玩得太开心了。

1088
00:43:10.820 --> 00:43:14.840
Well, when we go down to the warehouse again, I loved this moment.
嗯，当我们再次下到仓库时，我特别喜欢那个瞬间。

1089
00:43:15.200 --> 00:43:20.700
The scene when the sales guys are unpacking the truck, and Ryan says,
销售员们在卸货的那场戏，瑞安说，

1090
00:43:20.700 --> 00:43:24.300
you guys, we could get this job quicker if we form an assembly line.
伙计们，如果我们排成流水线，干活会更快。

1091
00:43:24.460 --> 00:43:28.620
And Stanley cuts him off and says, this is a run out the clock situation.
斯坦利打断他说，这情况就是为了磨洋工。

1092
00:43:28.620 --> 00:43:28.940
Yeah.
没错。

1093
00:43:29.400 --> 00:43:30.420
Just like upstairs.
跟楼上一样。

1094
00:43:30.740 --> 00:43:32.040
I'm going to break it down to you, kid.
小子，我给你拆解一下。

1095
00:43:32.340 --> 00:43:33.400
This is how we're doing this.
我们就是这么干活的。

1096
00:43:33.400 --> 00:43:37.440
We are not going to hypothesize on how to be more efficient.
我们不需要去假设怎么做效率更高。

1097
00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:39.680
This is just what gets done gets done.
这就是能干完多少就干多少。

1098
00:43:39.760 --> 00:43:40.620
Run out the clock.
磨洋工。

1099
00:43:40.740 --> 00:43:41.980
Run out the clock situation.
就是磨洋工的情况。

1100
00:43:42.420 --> 00:43:45.420
I was watching this with my daughter, and she goes, Mom, what does he mean?
我和我女儿一起看的时候，她问我，妈，他是什么意思？

1101
00:43:45.420 --> 00:43:49.740
And I said, Isabel, he wants to do the bare minimum, the bare minimum.
我说，伊莎贝尔，他只想做最起码的事，最起码的事。

1102
00:43:49.940 --> 00:43:51.780
She was like, I kind of get that.
她说，我有点理解。

1103
00:43:52.480 --> 00:43:53.240
I get it.
我懂。

1104
00:43:53.920 --> 00:43:56.140
I've been in a lot of run out the clock situations.
我经历过很多混时间的场合。

1105
00:43:56.940 --> 00:44:01.980
So when we go back upstairs, Jan starts explaining sports terMs.
所以当我们回到楼上时，简开始解释体育术语。

1106
00:44:02.240 --> 00:44:03.140
Sports metaphors.
体育隐喻。

1107
00:44:03.320 --> 00:44:03.820
To the women.
对女同事们。

1108
00:44:04.040 --> 00:44:05.620
It's how women might be left out in the workplace.
这是女性在职场中可能被排挤的方式。

1109
00:44:05.720 --> 00:44:07.640
I'm like, is this the 1950s?
我在想，现在是1950年代吗？

1110
00:44:07.660 --> 00:44:08.080
I know.
我知道。

1111
00:44:08.260 --> 00:44:09.500
This was so dated.
这太老套了。

1112
00:44:09.500 --> 00:44:15.220
This felt a little bit like it was out of some manual from 1953 or something.
感觉就像是出自1953年的某本手册之类的东西。

1113
00:44:15.420 --> 00:44:20.020
Well, at this point, Kelly pretends like she doesn't know what second base means.
嗯，这时候，凯莉假装不知道“二垒”是什么意思。

1114
00:44:20.400 --> 00:44:23.640
She says, okay, well, Michael said he got to second base with you.
她说，好吧，迈克尔说他和你有过二垒接触。

1115
00:44:23.720 --> 00:44:25.240
Does that mean you closed a sale?
那是指你完成了一笔交易吗？

1116
00:44:25.780 --> 00:44:27.500
Is that what second base means?
二垒是这个意思吗？

1117
00:44:27.700 --> 00:44:28.420
Guess what happened?
你猜发生了什么？

1118
00:44:28.420 --> 00:44:30.600
And this is a real rare thing.
这可是非常罕见的事情。

1119
00:44:30.740 --> 00:44:33.280
This is like seeing an albino rhino in the wild.
这就像在野外看到白化犀牛一样。

1120
00:44:33.480 --> 00:44:33.720
What?
什么？

1121
00:44:34.140 --> 00:44:35.300
Angela laughs.
安吉拉笑了。

1122
00:44:35.560 --> 00:44:36.000
Yes.
是的。

1123
00:44:36.520 --> 00:44:39.020
15 minutes, 10 seconds.
15分10秒。

1124
00:44:40.480 --> 00:44:42.440
Fan question from Jeff Ackerman.
来自杰夫·阿克曼的粉丝提问。

1125
00:44:42.640 --> 00:44:43.380
He pointed it out.
他指出了这一点。

1126
00:44:43.540 --> 00:44:49.300
There is a cutaway shot of Pam and Angela after Kelly plays dumb and asks Jan what second base means.
在凯莉装傻问简“二垒”是什么意思之后，有一个帕姆和安吉拉的切入镜头。

1127
00:44:49.480 --> 00:44:50.760
Was that scripted?
那是剧本写的吗？

1128
00:44:50.820 --> 00:44:53.420
Or was it so funny you couldn't keep a straight face?
还是因为太好笑了，你们没忍住笑场了？

1129
00:44:53.560 --> 00:44:55.760
That is me and Angela laughing.
那是我和安吉拉在笑。

1130
00:44:56.000 --> 00:44:56.760
We're laughing.
我们在笑。

1131
00:44:56.940 --> 00:44:57.360
We're laughing.
我们在笑。

1132
00:44:57.360 --> 00:45:06.040
But I also knew that my character really thought that Jan was just like, well, she says she looks whorish.
但我当时也知道，我的角色确实认为简看起来很……嗯，她说她看起来像个荡妇。

1133
00:45:06.280 --> 00:45:11.200
So she clearly doesn't think highly of Jan and judges her.
所以她显然对简评价不高，而且在评判她。

1134
00:45:11.400 --> 00:45:16.580
And so for Kelly to call her out, Angela thoroughly enjoyed that moment.
所以对于凯莉当众揭穿她，安吉拉非常享受那一刻。

1135
00:45:16.880 --> 00:45:18.720
I have an observation about this episode.
我对这一集有一个观察。

1136
00:45:18.720 --> 00:45:19.280
Oh, yes.
哦，好的。

1137
00:45:19.280 --> 00:45:22.620
And I'm going to get right up on my soapbox and shout it.
我要站上我的肥皂箱大声说出来。

1138
00:45:22.720 --> 00:45:23.860
Here we go.
开始了。

1139
00:45:23.860 --> 00:45:32.380
While re-watching this episode, I noticed that the people who are hardest on Jan and her ambition are other women.
在重看这一集时，我注意到对简和她的野心最苛刻的人其实是其他女性。

1140
00:45:32.520 --> 00:45:32.760
Yeah.
是的。

1141
00:45:33.220 --> 00:45:33.820
Other women.
其他女性。

1142
00:45:34.140 --> 00:45:36.440
Angela calls her a slut for the way she dresses.
安吉拉因为简的穿着说她是荡妇。

1143
00:45:36.760 --> 00:45:39.460
Pam is constantly rolling her eyes at her.
帕姆不断地对她翻白眼。

1144
00:45:39.640 --> 00:45:44.640
And then Kelly shames her slash embarrasses her for making out with Michael.
然后凯莉因为她和迈克尔亲热而羞辱她，让她难堪。

1145
00:45:44.900 --> 00:45:48.400
Then they lay into her for not being a mother.
接着她们又因为她没有当母亲而攻击她。

1146
00:45:48.920 --> 00:45:49.280
Yeah.
是的。

1147
00:45:49.280 --> 00:45:55.200
Oftentimes it is other women who make ambition hardest for women.
通常情况下，让女性的野心变得最艰难的，往往是其他女性。

1148
00:45:55.620 --> 00:46:02.560
I wondered if BJ intended to point this out or if it was a happy accident because you know what?
我想知道BJ是否有意指出这一点，还是这只是一个美丽的巧合，因为你知道吗？

1149
00:46:02.800 --> 00:46:05.080
Jan is so excited to help Pam.
简非常热衷于帮助帕姆。

1150
00:46:05.340 --> 00:46:08.740
She wants to help these other women rise up.
她想帮助这些女性提升自己。

1151
00:46:08.920 --> 00:46:09.980
She is so excited.
她太兴奋了。

1152
00:46:10.340 --> 00:46:16.920
Now, listen, I think that it is totally valid when Phyllis says, I'm happy with my choices.
听着，我觉得菲利斯说“我对自己的选择很满意”时，这完全是合情合理的。

1153
00:46:16.920 --> 00:46:17.420
Yeah.
没错。

1154
00:46:17.420 --> 00:46:18.620
We don't all need to be you.
我们不需要都活成你那样。

1155
00:46:18.820 --> 00:46:23.360
Not all women or all people need to be ambitious or share ambitions.
并非所有的女性或所有人都有必要野心勃勃，或者拥有相同的抱负。

1156
00:46:24.180 --> 00:46:30.140
But they are really hard on her and unaccepting of her for wanting to be her.
但大家对她太苛刻了，不能接受她只想做她自己。

1157
00:46:30.860 --> 00:46:33.540
Like, Phyllis is like, I'm going to be me.
就像菲利斯说的那样，我要做我自己。

1158
00:46:33.940 --> 00:46:36.180
But then they're kind of hard on Jan for being Jan.
但他们对简做简自己这件事又有点苛刻。

1159
00:46:36.440 --> 00:46:40.300
Well, I think Phyllis is probably the most fair of everyone.
嗯，我觉得菲利斯可能是所有人里最公正的一个了。

1160
00:46:40.540 --> 00:46:40.860
True.
确实。

1161
00:46:40.860 --> 00:46:48.360
She's really happy with her life choices and stands by them and is unapologetic and has a very happy life.
她对自己的生活选择感到非常幸福，坚持自己的选择，从不感到抱歉，而且过着非常幸福的生活。

1162
00:46:48.540 --> 00:46:54.360
And I don't think that she wishes for Jan not to have anything.
而且我不认为她希望简一无所有。

1163
00:46:54.580 --> 00:46:57.000
I think Phyllis is happy that Jan has chosen her path.
我觉得菲利斯很高兴简选择了自己的道路。

1164
00:46:57.120 --> 00:47:00.900
But everyone else in the room is snarky towards Jan.
但房间里的其他人对简都很刻薄。

1165
00:47:01.040 --> 00:47:01.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1166
00:47:01.160 --> 00:47:01.680
They are.
确实如此。

1167
00:47:01.920 --> 00:47:06.380
And I think one of the things I love about our friendship,
我觉得我们的友谊中我最喜欢的一点是，

1168
00:47:06.700 --> 00:47:15.800
and you and I both have like a group of female friends who are really about supporting one another and building each other up and encouraging each other.
你和我都有一个女性朋友群体，大家真的都在互相支持、互相成就、互相鼓励。

1169
00:47:15.980 --> 00:47:18.940
And you really need those women in your life.
你生命中真的需要这样的女性。

1170
00:47:19.060 --> 00:47:19.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1171
00:47:19.520 --> 00:47:20.560
You really do.
真的需要。

1172
00:47:20.560 --> 00:47:21.120
Yeah.
没错。

1173
00:47:21.680 --> 00:47:28.660
Because that really, the momentum that women give one another is really the momentum that moves us forward.
因为那种女性之间给予彼此的动力，确实是推动我们前进的动力。

1174
00:47:28.880 --> 00:47:29.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1175
00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:30.280
Mostly.
大多时候是这样。

1176
00:47:30.580 --> 00:47:32.100
All right, Jenna, step on down.
好了，珍娜，下来吧。

1177
00:47:32.380 --> 00:47:32.900
I'm stepping down.
我下来了。

1178
00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:33.480
Step down.
下来吧。

1179
00:47:33.620 --> 00:47:34.120
I like it.
我喜欢。

1180
00:47:34.160 --> 00:47:35.100
I like what you had to say.
我喜欢你刚才说的话。

1181
00:47:35.380 --> 00:47:35.740
All right.
好吧。

1182
00:47:35.860 --> 00:47:36.860
I'm off my soapbox.
我发表完高论了。

1183
00:47:36.880 --> 00:47:44.000
Well, here's a juxtaposition to your soapbox moment, which I thought was really just well said.
好吧，和你刚才那番高论形成鲜明对比的是，我觉得你刚才说得真好。

1184
00:47:44.220 --> 00:47:44.560
Thanks.
谢谢。

1185
00:47:44.780 --> 00:47:47.400
Here's at 15 minutes, 59 seconds.
这是在15分59秒处。

1186
00:47:47.520 --> 00:47:47.700
Yep.
没错。

1187
00:47:47.700 --> 00:47:50.260
Michael puts packing peanuts into a fan.
迈克尔把包装用的泡沫颗粒扔进了风扇里。

1188
00:47:50.520 --> 00:47:51.180
What a dick.
真是个混蛋。

1189
00:47:52.000 --> 00:47:53.220
That's what I had to say.
这就是我想说的。

1190
00:47:53.400 --> 00:47:54.520
That's my deep thought.
这就是我的深刻见解。

1191
00:47:55.600 --> 00:48:00.120
Well, Jan gets so annoyed that she goes down to the warehouse.
简被气得去了仓库。

1192
00:48:00.440 --> 00:48:00.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1193
00:48:00.840 --> 00:48:06.860
And this is when Jan tells the warehouse that if they unionize, they're all going to lose their jobs.
就在这时，简告诉仓库员工，如果他们成立工会，他们都会丢掉工作。

1194
00:48:07.000 --> 00:48:07.160
Right.
没错。

1195
00:48:07.380 --> 00:48:09.660
Very, very, very anti-union.
非常、非常、非常反工会。

1196
00:48:09.660 --> 00:48:11.940
Yes, and I read, actually,
是的，而且我读到过，

1197
00:48:12.080 --> 00:48:28.480
that this episode has been used in law classes that deal with companies who have unions and who want to form unions and that it has been used to show the pressure and the hard road that they can have in those moments.
这一集被用在法律课上，专门讨论那些有工会或想要成立工会的公司，用来展示在那种时刻他们所面临的压力和艰难处境。

1198
00:48:28.480 --> 00:48:33.360
All right, guys, we're going to get into some sad times now for Jim and Pam.
好了，各位，现在我们要进入吉姆和帕姆的悲伤时刻了。

1199
00:48:33.960 --> 00:48:34.140
Ooh.
噢。

1200
00:48:34.560 --> 00:48:35.120
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1201
00:48:35.380 --> 00:48:35.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1202
00:48:35.960 --> 00:48:37.640
Jim comes upstairs to make a phone call.
吉姆上楼去打了个电话。

1203
00:48:37.900 --> 00:48:45.840
Pam excuses herself from her meeting, and she very excitedly tells Jim about this internship opportunity in graphic design.
帕姆找借口离开了会议，非常兴奋地告诉吉姆关于这个平面设计的实习机会。

1204
00:48:46.560 --> 00:48:49.220
Jim adorably encourages her immediately.
吉姆立刻可爱地鼓励了她。

1205
00:48:49.400 --> 00:48:51.480
He's like, well, what are the details?
他就像是说，嗯，具体细节是什么？

1206
00:48:51.480 --> 00:48:52.340
I think you should do it.
我觉得你应该去。

1207
00:48:52.620 --> 00:48:53.080
I know.
我知道。

1208
00:48:53.500 --> 00:48:54.920
And she just lights up.
然后她整个人都亮了起来。

1209
00:48:55.100 --> 00:49:00.580
She needed someone to give her permission in a way to go for this.
她在某种程度上需要有人给她许可去追求这个机会。

1210
00:49:00.800 --> 00:49:00.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1211
00:49:01.060 --> 00:49:02.540
And Jim immediately did.
而吉姆立刻就给了她。

1212
00:49:02.700 --> 00:49:02.960
Yes.
没错。

1213
00:49:02.960 --> 00:49:03.720
Because he's her soulmate.
因为他是她的灵魂伴侣。

1214
00:49:03.960 --> 00:49:04.300
Yes.
是的。

1215
00:49:05.900 --> 00:49:10.420
So you kind of get the sense she's going to go for it, but then you see a scene.
所以你会有种感觉她会去尝试，但随后你看到了一个场景。

1216
00:49:10.540 --> 00:49:11.600
It's a spy shot.
那是一个偷拍镜头。

1217
00:49:11.760 --> 00:49:12.520
There's no dialogue.
没有对话。

1218
00:49:12.780 --> 00:49:14.040
She's holding the pamphlet.
她拿着宣传册。

1219
00:49:14.460 --> 00:49:19.980
She's telling Roy about the program, and it's very clear that he is not supportive.
她正在告诉罗伊关于这个项目的事，很明显他并不支持。

1220
00:49:19.980 --> 00:49:21.600
He sees it as a waste of time.
他觉得这是在浪费时间。

1221
00:49:21.740 --> 00:49:26.340
So we cut to this Pam talking head, and she starts talking about this house with a terrace.
所以我们切到了帕姆的采访镜头，她开始谈论那个带露台的房子。

1222
00:49:26.840 --> 00:49:28.540
Oh, this house with a terrace.
噢，那个带露台的房子。

1223
00:49:28.760 --> 00:49:31.940
This metaphor broke my heart.
这个隐喻让我心碎。

1224
00:49:32.260 --> 00:49:32.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1225
00:49:32.940 --> 00:49:38.780
She says she was a little girl, and she read this book, and there was a house with a terrace with flowers.
她说她小时候读过一本书，里面有一栋带花卉露台的房子。

1226
00:49:39.440 --> 00:49:43.880
And she describes it in detail, and she says, I just always wanted that.
她详细地描述了它，然后说，我一直都想要那个。

1227
00:49:44.000 --> 00:49:46.920
But, you know, it's just, you know.
但是，你知道，就是，你知道的。

1228
00:49:47.180 --> 00:49:49.920
They don't even have those kind of houses in Scranton.
斯克兰顿根本就没有那种房子。

1229
00:49:50.800 --> 00:49:53.820
Well, this was based on a story of mine.
嗯，这是基于我的一个故事。

1230
00:49:55.120 --> 00:49:56.800
BJ came up to me on the set.
B.J. 在片场找到我。

1231
00:49:56.940 --> 00:49:58.180
We were working on a different episode.
我们当时在拍另一集。

1232
00:49:58.180 --> 00:50:04.460
He was writing this episode, and he came up to me, and he said, Jenna, I've got this moment I'm trying to write.
他在写这一集，他走过来对我说，珍娜，我有个片段想写。

1233
00:50:04.940 --> 00:50:15.060
Was there ever a dream that you had as a little girl that has gone unrealized because it seemed unrealistic to you?
你小时候有没有什么梦想，因为觉得不切实际而一直没能实现？

1234
00:50:15.280 --> 00:50:17.200
He said it can be really simple, though.
他说其实可以很简单。

1235
00:50:17.200 --> 00:50:18.720
It's a little girl's dream.
就是一个小女孩的梦想。

1236
00:50:19.620 --> 00:50:21.280
And I said yes.
我说有。

1237
00:50:21.540 --> 00:50:22.980
How smart is that, though?
这不是很聪明吗？

1238
00:50:23.120 --> 00:50:23.440
I know.
我知道。

1239
00:50:23.600 --> 00:50:24.700
BJ is so smart.
B.J. 太聪明了。

1240
00:50:24.800 --> 00:50:26.100
Isn't that such a great question?
这不是一个很棒的问题吗？

1241
00:50:26.200 --> 00:50:27.160
It's so wonderful.
太美妙了。

1242
00:50:27.420 --> 00:50:31.420
Writers, most of their job is just asking the right questions.
编剧们，他们大部分的工作就是问对问题。

1243
00:50:31.740 --> 00:50:33.080
BJ is so smart.
B.J. 太聪明了。

1244
00:50:33.080 --> 00:50:35.020
Okay, so what your answer was?
好吧，那你的回答是什么？

1245
00:50:35.280 --> 00:50:36.160
My answer was yes.
我的回答是有。

1246
00:50:36.300 --> 00:50:39.040
When I was younger, I read this book.
我小时候读过一本书。

1247
00:50:39.260 --> 00:50:45.700
And in the book, there was a girl who moved into a new house with her family, and the house had a tower.
书里有个女孩随家人搬进了一栋新房子，那房子有个塔楼。

1248
00:50:46.680 --> 00:50:55.840
Sort of like a castle might, it was this tower room on the side of the house, and there was one set of stairs that went up to it.
就像城堡那样，房子侧面有个塔楼房间，有一段楼梯通往那里。

1249
00:50:55.940 --> 00:51:01.100
And so there was this one circular room on the third floor of their home.
所以在那栋房子的三楼有一个圆形的房间。

1250
00:51:01.100 --> 00:51:07.020
And this was her space that she declared was hers to sit and think and create.
那是她宣布属于自己的空间，可以在那里坐着、思考和创作。

1251
00:51:08.120 --> 00:51:12.820
And I had such a clear vision of what this tower room was.
我当时对这个塔楼房间有着非常清晰的构想。

1252
00:51:12.960 --> 00:51:20.200
And I remember thinking to myself, one day, I'm going to have a house with a circular tower room where I will create.
我记得当时心想，总有一天，我要拥有一栋带圆形塔楼房间的房子，在那里进行创作。

1253
00:51:21.300 --> 00:51:25.700
And I've never had it, and I never got it, because who builds houses like that?
但我从来没拥有过，也一直没实现，毕竟谁会盖那样的房子呢？

1254
00:51:25.980 --> 00:51:28.220
I think this dream, do not let it go.
我觉得这个梦想，不要放弃。

1255
00:51:28.400 --> 00:51:28.800
I think.
我是这么想的。

1256
00:51:28.920 --> 00:51:29.720
Maybe one day.
也许总有一天吧。

1257
00:51:29.720 --> 00:51:35.040
One day, maybe, you know, they'll be like, you know, Jenna Fisher, she lives in a tower.
也许有一天，人们会说，你看，珍娜·费舍，她住在一座塔楼里。

1258
00:51:36.060 --> 00:51:41.800
She has a very normal-looking house, and then next to it, she has built this tower.
她住着一栋看起来很普通的房子，然后在旁边盖了这么一座塔楼。

1259
00:51:42.560 --> 00:51:43.040
In Missouri.
在密苏里州。

1260
00:51:43.740 --> 00:51:44.720
It's very strange.
这太奇怪了。

1261
00:51:45.400 --> 00:51:51.740
So BJ ran with that story, and that was, he adapted it, and he made it a terrace with flowers.
所以BJ采用了这个故事，他进行了改编，把它变成了一个种满鲜花的露台。

1262
00:51:53.020 --> 00:51:56.260
But that was a little bit of collaboration there.
但那里面确实有一点点合作的成分。

1263
00:51:56.260 --> 00:51:59.160
I think it's such a sweet story, and then it broke my heart.
我觉得这是一个很温馨的故事，但后来它又让我心碎了。

1264
00:51:59.460 --> 00:52:01.860
Well, Pam then is in the kitchen with Jim.
嗯，帕姆当时和吉姆在厨房里。

1265
00:52:02.260 --> 00:52:05.160
Her talking head is kind of broken up by this scene in the kitchen.
她的单人访谈被厨房里的这一幕给打断了。

1266
00:52:05.700 --> 00:52:10.780
And she's saying to Jim, Jim is like, wait, you're not going to take the internship?
她对吉姆说，吉姆当时问，等等，你不打算去实习了吗？

1267
00:52:10.780 --> 00:52:16.320
And she's like, well, you know, like Roy said, there's no guarantee it's going to lead to anything anyway.
她说，嗯，你知道的，就像罗伊说的，反正也没保证这能带来什么结果。

1268
00:52:16.580 --> 00:52:17.680
He's like, Roy said that?
吉姆问，罗伊真这么说？

1269
00:52:18.060 --> 00:52:20.960
And then Pam flips a switch.
然后帕姆的态度突然变了。

1270
00:52:21.060 --> 00:52:22.680
She's like, oh, do you have something to say?
她说，哦，你有什么话想说吗？

1271
00:52:22.820 --> 00:52:25.240
I was like, oh, dang, here we go.
我当时心想，哦，糟糕，要开始了。

1272
00:52:25.460 --> 00:52:26.080
I know.
我知道。

1273
00:52:26.600 --> 00:52:27.400
She's hurt.
她受伤了。

1274
00:52:27.600 --> 00:52:28.420
She's hurt.
她受伤了。

1275
00:52:29.040 --> 00:52:30.640
And it's not Jim's fault.
而且这不是吉姆的错。

1276
00:52:30.660 --> 00:52:32.360
He's speaking truth, you know?
他是在说实话，你知道吗？

1277
00:52:32.460 --> 00:52:32.520
I know.
我知道。

1278
00:52:32.660 --> 00:52:33.500
But he's holding that.
但他一直在坚持这一点。

1279
00:52:33.500 --> 00:52:35.200
She's like, I'm happy with my choices.
她说，我对自己的选择很满意。

1280
00:52:35.660 --> 00:52:37.300
He's holding that mirror up.
他是在拿镜子照她。

1281
00:52:37.380 --> 00:52:38.660
That's what he does to her.
这就是他对她所做的事。

1282
00:52:38.660 --> 00:52:40.940
Yeah, I know.
是啊，我知道。

1283
00:52:41.720 --> 00:52:44.120
This is an interesting fan question.
这是一个有趣的粉丝提问。

1284
00:52:44.760 --> 00:52:49.200
Bernardo noted that Jim has a beard when he's talking to Pam in the kitchen.
贝尔纳多指出，吉姆在厨房和帕姆说话时留着胡茬。

1285
00:52:49.200 --> 00:52:50.800
And I looked, and he really does.
我仔细看了看，他还真是。

1286
00:52:50.960 --> 00:52:52.380
He's like very stubbly.
他看起来胡子拉碴的。

1287
00:52:52.600 --> 00:52:53.020
What?
什么？

1288
00:52:53.360 --> 00:52:55.120
So just to break up that beautiful moment.
所以这正好破坏了那个美好的时刻。

1289
00:52:55.440 --> 00:53:02.280
Well, Jim says something that really stuck with me, which is he says, you got to take a chance on something sometime.
嗯，吉姆说了一句让我印象深刻的话，他说，你总得在某个时候冒个险。

1290
00:53:02.700 --> 00:53:03.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1291
00:53:03.520 --> 00:53:06.180
And I thought that was like just a good thing to take away.
我觉得这是一个很好的感悟。

1292
00:53:06.880 --> 00:53:13.780
Well, we go back to the talking head, and Pam just breaks down.
嗯，我们回到单人访谈，帕姆彻底崩溃了。

1293
00:53:14.080 --> 00:53:17.340
She's talking about the terrorists, but we know what she's really talking about.
她谈论的是露台，但我们都知道她真正想说的是什么。

1294
00:53:17.940 --> 00:53:20.000
She says it's just not practical.
她说这根本不切实际。

1295
00:53:20.420 --> 00:53:23.180
You know, you just aren't going to find that.
你知道，你就是找不到那种东西。

1296
00:53:23.280 --> 00:53:28.080
And what she's really saying is, I'm never going to have Jim.
而她真正想说的是，我永远也得不到吉姆。

1297
00:53:28.340 --> 00:53:30.020
I'm never going to have true love.
我永远也得不到真爱。

1298
00:53:30.320 --> 00:53:32.220
I'm never going to be who I want to be.
我永远也无法成为我想成为的人。

1299
00:53:32.860 --> 00:53:35.240
And that's underneath all of that.
所有这一切之下隐藏的正是这些。

1300
00:53:35.380 --> 00:53:37.620
And also that my dreams aren't valid.
还有就是，我的梦想是不被认可的。

1301
00:53:38.160 --> 00:53:38.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1302
00:53:38.800 --> 00:53:40.540
I don't get to even try for my dream.
我甚至连追求梦想的机会都没有。

1303
00:53:40.780 --> 00:53:42.020
That's not my path.
那不是我的人生轨迹。

1304
00:53:42.220 --> 00:53:44.140
A fan question from Adam Falk.
来自亚当·福尔克的粉丝提问。

1305
00:53:44.380 --> 00:53:48.060
He asked, when Roy killed Pam's dream, the tears were so real.
他问，当罗伊扼杀帕姆的梦想时，那些眼泪看起来太真实了。

1306
00:53:48.320 --> 00:53:49.460
What were you thinking about?
你当时在想什么？

1307
00:53:50.560 --> 00:53:55.720
Guys, there are times as an actor where your heart just breaks for your character.
伙计们，作为演员，有时你会真心为你的角色感到心碎。

1308
00:53:56.800 --> 00:54:02.380
I just felt her heartbreaking, and it made me cry.
我当时感受到了她的心碎，这让我流泪了。

1309
00:54:02.580 --> 00:54:06.360
It's in the same way where it makes you cry when you watch something.
就像你看某些东西时会流泪一样。

1310
00:54:06.520 --> 00:54:07.800
Or talk about it.
或者谈论它的时候。

1311
00:54:07.920 --> 00:54:08.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1312
00:54:08.560 --> 00:54:13.400
I wasn't thinking about, you know, my dead pet or something like that.
我当时并没有在想什么死去的宠物之类的东西。

1313
00:54:13.400 --> 00:54:24.400
I was thinking about how it must feel to have someone not encourage you to feel trapped and to feel so alone.
我是在想，当有人不支持你，让你感到被困住、感到如此孤独时，那会是什么感觉。

1314
00:54:24.400 --> 00:54:31.480
And I thought about how the one person who was trying to help me, I just pushed that person away.
我想到那个试图帮助我的人，而我却把他推开了。

1315
00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:34.060
And that kind of makes you cry.
那种感觉真的会让人流泪。

1316
00:54:34.520 --> 00:54:40.640
Well, I think our show had a lot of, like, really relatable moments like that.
嗯，我觉得我们的剧里有很多那种让人感同身受的时刻。

1317
00:54:40.780 --> 00:54:42.660
I mean, I know we do these crazy things.
我是说，我知道我们做了很多疯狂的事。

1318
00:54:42.660 --> 00:54:48.180
Like, it's going to cut to the warehouse, and Dwight is making a snow angel out of packing peanuts, and there's all of that.
比如，镜头切到仓库，德怀特正用包装泡沫颗粒做雪天使，诸如此类。

1319
00:54:48.180 --> 00:54:54.160
But then I feel like the heart of our show is also just these people living their lives and relationships.
但我觉得我们剧的核心也正是这些人过着他们的生活，处理着人际关系。

1320
00:54:54.240 --> 00:54:56.660
And I love that we have that balance.
我很喜欢这种平衡。

1321
00:54:56.900 --> 00:54:57.420
Me too.
我也是。

1322
00:54:58.060 --> 00:55:03.540
Well, speaking of the warehouse, we cut back down to the warehouse, and Michael has completely destroyed it.
说到仓库，镜头切回仓库，迈克尔把它彻底毁了。

1323
00:55:03.980 --> 00:55:04.960
He's wrecked it.
他把它搞得一团糟。

1324
00:55:05.060 --> 00:55:05.520
Wrecked it.
搞得一团糟。

1325
00:55:05.580 --> 00:55:07.680
And then he just buys pizza for everyone and leaves.
然后他给每个人买了披萨就走了。

1326
00:55:07.780 --> 00:55:08.360
You know why?
你知道为什么吗？

1327
00:55:08.500 --> 00:55:10.320
Because pizza is the great equalizer.
因为披萨是伟大的平衡器。

1328
00:55:10.320 --> 00:55:10.860
Equalizer.
平衡器。

1329
00:55:11.580 --> 00:55:12.640
That's what he says.
他是这么说的。

1330
00:55:12.660 --> 00:55:14.320
It's the great equalizer.
它是伟大的平衡器。

1331
00:55:14.520 --> 00:55:18.040
Well, fan question from Tiffany Ironridge and Pickle Dude.
嗯，来自蒂芙尼·艾恩里奇和“泡菜老兄”的粉丝提问。

1332
00:55:18.400 --> 00:55:20.980
How long did it take to clean up the warehouse?
清理仓库花了多长时间？

1333
00:55:21.480 --> 00:55:25.660
And Madeline Albrecht, I feel like this is because she listens to Office Ladies, says,
还有马德琳·阿尔布雷希特，我觉得她是因为听了《办公室女士》播客才问的，她说：

1334
00:55:25.780 --> 00:55:28.420
was it a hard day for Phil Shea and Michael Gallenberg?
这对菲尔·谢和迈克尔·加伦伯格来说是艰难的一天吗？

1335
00:55:28.780 --> 00:55:30.140
Oh, I love you.
哦，我爱你。

1336
00:55:30.140 --> 00:55:33.580
And I bet they love you too for just even highlighting that.
我敢说他们也爱你，因为你甚至提到了这一点。

1337
00:55:33.800 --> 00:55:36.340
Gina McAdrian said, who cleaned up the mess?
吉娜·麦克阿德里安问，是谁清理了烂摊子？

1338
00:55:36.340 --> 00:55:37.520
Guys, it was.
伙计们，是他们。

1339
00:55:37.520 --> 00:55:40.320
It was Phil Shea, Michael Gallenberg, their crews.
是菲尔·谢、迈克尔·加伦伯格和他们的团队。

1340
00:55:40.720 --> 00:55:41.120
Their crews.
他们的团队。

1341
00:55:41.120 --> 00:55:44.420
I don't know how long it took them, but I imagine a long time.
我不知道花了他们多久，但我猜肯定很久。

1342
00:55:44.580 --> 00:55:48.180
And also, I think these kind of shoots were more stressful for them because there were
而且，我觉得这种拍摄对他们来说压力更大，因为有

1343
00:55:48.180 --> 00:55:52.860
big prop moments that the whole scene was centered around.
重要的道具时刻，整个场景都围绕着这些道具展开。

1344
00:55:53.080 --> 00:55:55.120
And they had to have everything ready.
他们必须把一切准备就绪。

1345
00:55:55.460 --> 00:55:59.260
When Michael opened up the bag of packing peanuts, they had to have a backup one.
当迈克尔打开那袋包装泡沫颗粒时，他们必须准备好备用的。

1346
00:55:59.440 --> 00:56:01.320
They had to have all that ready to go.
他们必须确保一切准备就绪。

1347
00:56:01.500 --> 00:56:03.560
If you get a chance, watch the deleted scenes.
如果有机会，去看看删减片段。

1348
00:56:03.560 --> 00:56:06.980
There is one that I loved so much in this.
这一集里有一个片段我非常喜欢。

1349
00:56:07.120 --> 00:56:10.560
It has nothing to do with this episode, really, the story at all.
它其实和这一集的故事没什么关系。

1350
00:56:11.440 --> 00:56:13.660
Michael is trying to set his ringtone.
迈克尔正试图设置他的手机铃声。

1351
00:56:14.060 --> 00:56:17.360
Oh, and he's asking Pam to help him pick a ringtone.
哦，他还让帕姆帮他选手机铃声。

1352
00:56:17.540 --> 00:56:18.620
Yes, and Jim is there too.
对，吉姆也在那儿。

1353
00:56:18.780 --> 00:56:22.940
And it's just these little small ridiculous moments that crack me up.
就是这些微小又荒唐的瞬间让我笑个不停。

1354
00:56:23.060 --> 00:56:25.280
We had a lot of those that we would shoot.
我们拍过很多这样的片段。

1355
00:56:25.440 --> 00:56:27.500
They were just office life moments.
它们只是办公室生活的点滴。

1356
00:56:27.720 --> 00:56:27.880
Yeah.
没错。

1357
00:56:28.020 --> 00:56:31.300
And so often, those were the things that would have to get cut for time.
但往往为了控制时长，这些片段不得不被剪掉。

1358
00:56:31.300 --> 00:56:31.980
I know.
我知道。

1359
00:56:31.980 --> 00:56:36.020
But they're now a treasure living on the DVD extras.
不过它们现在成了DVD花絮里的珍宝。

1360
00:56:37.140 --> 00:56:45.020
At 19 minutes, 52 seconds, I want you to notice, we imply that everyone from the warehouse
在19分52秒的时候，请注意，我们暗示仓库里的所有人

1361
00:56:45.020 --> 00:56:46.240
is walking back upstairs.
正走回楼上。

1362
00:56:46.240 --> 00:56:51.120
I want you to notice that just Michael, Kevin, and Dwight go into the door at the top of the
请注意，只有迈克尔、凯文和德怀特走进了楼梯顶端的

1363
00:56:51.120 --> 00:56:51.460
stairs.
那扇门。

1364
00:56:52.140 --> 00:56:56.080
That's, again, because it's just a closet, and that was as many people as they could fit.
那是因为那其实只是个壁橱，只能挤下那么多人。

1365
00:56:56.160 --> 00:56:56.340
Right.
没错。

1366
00:56:56.460 --> 00:56:57.240
And that was tight.
而且当时很挤。

1367
00:56:57.240 --> 00:57:02.220
And then in the next shot, you see them walking into the office.
然后在下一个镜头里，你看到他们走进了办公室。

1368
00:57:02.380 --> 00:57:03.560
Michael's carrying a pizza.
迈克尔提着披萨。

1369
00:57:04.180 --> 00:57:07.040
But we shot that on a completely different day.
但我们是在完全不同的一天拍的那个镜头。

1370
00:57:07.340 --> 00:57:07.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1371
00:57:07.760 --> 00:57:13.880
So Veda, our script supervisor, she would have written down which hand Michael was carrying
所以我们的场记维达会记下迈克尔是用哪只手提着

1372
00:57:13.880 --> 00:57:20.100
the pizza box in so that she could hand him that pizza box then on the next day and say,
披萨盒的，这样第二天她就能把披萨盒递给他并说，

1373
00:57:20.240 --> 00:57:21.120
all right, here it is.
好了，给你。

1374
00:57:21.120 --> 00:57:24.340
Although sometimes they would have conversations that were like, well, I could believe that
虽然有时我们也会讨论，比如，嗯，我可以相信

1375
00:57:24.340 --> 00:57:26.360
you switched hands on the way up.
你在上楼途中换了手。

1376
00:57:26.540 --> 00:57:27.480
We would have deep conversations.
我们会进行深入的探讨。

1377
00:57:27.780 --> 00:57:28.320
We would have deep conversations.
我们会进行深入的探讨。

1378
00:57:28.560 --> 00:57:32.120
Do you think he switched the pizza box from one hand to the other while he was walking?
你觉得他在走路的时候把披萨盒从一只手换到了另一只手吗？

1379
00:57:32.280 --> 00:57:34.240
Because maybe you had to use that hand to open the door.
因为也许他得腾出手来开门。

1380
00:57:34.440 --> 00:57:34.640
Yes.
是的。

1381
00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:35.360
Exactly.
没错。

1382
00:57:35.560 --> 00:57:35.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1383
00:57:35.920 --> 00:57:36.160
Exactly.
没错。

1384
00:57:36.180 --> 00:57:37.200
So perhaps, you know what?
所以也许，你知道吗？

1385
00:57:37.220 --> 00:57:37.560
It's fine.
没关系。

1386
00:57:37.640 --> 00:57:38.840
You can carry it in either hand.
你可以用哪只手提都行。

1387
00:57:38.840 --> 00:57:44.240
Well, I was really bummed that at the Women in the Workplace, there was no food because
嗯，我真的很失望在“职场女性”那集里没有吃的，因为

1388
00:57:44.240 --> 00:57:47.080
I was really excited that we might have pizza too.
我本来很兴奋，以为我们也能有披萨吃。

1389
00:57:48.320 --> 00:57:49.560
I mean, you know.
我是说，你知道的。

1390
00:57:49.560 --> 00:57:51.480
This was Jan's big fail.
这是简的一次重大失误。

1391
00:57:51.620 --> 00:57:53.000
If she would have just fed us.
如果她当时能给我们提供食物的话。

1392
00:57:53.320 --> 00:57:54.260
Snacks or something.
零食什么的。

1393
00:57:54.580 --> 00:57:58.120
But, you know, Mindy and I, Ed Helms, we love prop food.
不过，你知道，敏迪、我和艾德·赫尔姆斯，我们都很喜欢道具食物。

1394
00:57:59.580 --> 00:58:04.200
Well, this episode ends with Pam answering the phone.
嗯，这一集以帕姆接电话结束。

1395
00:58:04.400 --> 00:58:06.120
Dunder Mifflin, this is Pam.
邓德·米福林，我是帕姆。

1396
00:58:06.120 --> 00:58:10.200
And this is really significant because in her fight with Jim, he says to her,
这意义重大，因为在和吉姆吵架时，他对她说，

1397
00:58:10.460 --> 00:58:12.800
what, do you really want to be a receptionist your whole life?
怎么，你真的想当一辈子前台吗？

1398
00:58:13.300 --> 00:58:16.600
And so we end with her being a receptioniSt.
所以我们以她依然在前台工作作为结尾。

1399
00:58:16.760 --> 00:58:18.780
And she just looks at him.
而她只是看着他。

1400
00:58:18.980 --> 00:58:19.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1401
00:58:19.480 --> 00:58:20.260
There's this moment.
有这么一个时刻。

1402
00:58:20.540 --> 00:58:21.680
It's unresolved.
它悬而未决。

1403
00:58:21.880 --> 00:58:23.140
Their fight is unresolved.
他们的争吵悬而未决。

1404
00:58:23.340 --> 00:58:24.200
And that's it.
就是这样。

1405
00:58:24.260 --> 00:58:25.180
That's boys and girls.
这就是男孩和女孩。

1406
00:58:25.440 --> 00:58:26.860
Now, we have a fan requeSt.
现在，我们有一个粉丝请求。

1407
00:58:27.120 --> 00:58:27.980
Let me know what you think.
让我知道你们怎么看。

1408
00:58:28.300 --> 00:58:34.520
CG wrote in to say, I would really love for you guys to keep track, because we've been
CG写信来说，我真的很希望你们能留意一下，因为我们一直在

1409
00:58:34.520 --> 00:58:35.380
tracking things.
追踪这些事情。

1410
00:58:35.560 --> 00:58:35.680
Yeah.
没错。

1411
